<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Hancock</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1712</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Hancock was a Tuscarora leader in North Carolina, chief of the southern Tuscarora towns around Catechna. Angered by settler encroachment, land seizures and the enslavement of their people, his warriors attacked the colonial settlements on the Neuse and Pamlico rivers in September 1711, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a>, and executed the surveyor John Lawson. He was later captured by the rival chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tom-blount">Tom Blount</a> and handed to the colonists, who executed him in 1712.</p></div>
